IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g1-licensing-duty`
IMPORT `g1-adverse-action`
IMPORT `g3-training-duty`
IMPORT `g4-council-work`

-- int-council.l4: integration point IP7.  "The Council was consulted, and its advice was validly given" is group 4's answer (ss.24 to 26:
-- a request was made, and the advice is the Council's decision carried at a quorate meeting, or the delegated advice of a subcommittee
-- on an individual matter).  Groups 1 and 3 take the two halves as BOOLEAN fields of their own records.  The wrappers below build
-- those records from the facts of the case and a `Consultation of the Council`, so the two halves cannot be set by hand to disagree
-- with the Council's own rules.
--
-- Assumed, not ruled: which function of s.26(a) each consultation falls under.  Group 4 lets a subcommittee give valid advice only on
-- function (3), so the choice matters for a consultation whose advice came from a subcommittee.  The integrator's mapping, which the
-- caller overrides by building the consultation itself, is: an exemption order under s.3(b) is function (1); the measures of s.10, the
-- course required under s.17(b), the extension of s.17(c) and the recognition of a foreign qualification under s.19(c) concern an
-- individual licensee or applicant and are function (3).  s.26(a)(3) lists by name the recognition of a foreign qualification, the refusal
-- to renew, the conditioning of renewal on training, revocation, restriction, suspension and the extension of validity; it does not name
-- the requirement of a particular course under s.17(b) (group 3, contradiction C10), which may therefore be function (4), "any other
-- function the Law gives the Council", where a subcommittee's advice is not the Council's.  The consultation for a course is therefore the
-- caller's to build; `int — a consultation on another function whose advice came from` builds the function (4) reading.  The helpers
-- `int — a consultation on ...` build such consultations.

§ `Integration point IP7: the Council's advice`

§§ `A consultation of the Council, as the integrator builds one`

@ref Law s.26(a)(3), s.24 to 26 (IP7)
@desc A consultation about an individual licensee or applicant (function (3) of s.26(a)): a request was made, and the advice came from the source given
GIVEN source IS A `Source of the Council's advice`
GIVETH A `Consultation of the Council`
`int — a consultation on an individual matter whose advice came from` source MEANS
    `Consultation of the Council` WITH
        `the function the consultation falls under` IS `function (3): advising the Registrar on individual applications and decisions`
        `a request for the Council's advice was made` IS TRUE
        `the source of the advice, if any has been given` IS JUST source

@ref Law s.26(a)(1), s.3(b), s.24 to 26 (IP7)
@desc A consultation about an exemption from licensing (function (1) of s.26(a)): a request was made, and the advice came from the source given
GIVEN source IS A `Source of the Council's advice`
GIVETH A `Consultation of the Council`
`int — a consultation on an exemption whose advice came from` source MEANS
    `Consultation of the Council` WITH
        `the function the consultation falls under` IS `function (1): advising the Minister on exemption from licensing`
        `a request for the Council's advice was made` IS TRUE
        `the source of the advice, if any has been given` IS JUST source

@ref Law s.26(a)(4), s.17(b), s.24 to 26 (IP7; group 3 contradiction C10)
@desc A consultation about any other function the Law gives the Council (function (4) of s.26(a)): a request was made, and the advice came from the source given; a subcommittee's advice is not the Council's here
GIVEN source IS A `Source of the Council's advice`
GIVETH A `Consultation of the Council`
`int — a consultation on another function whose advice came from` source MEANS
    `Consultation of the Council` WITH
        `the function the consultation falls under` IS `function (4): any other function the Law gives the Council`
        `a request for the Council's advice was made` IS TRUE
        `the source of the advice, if any has been given` IS JUST source

@ref Law s.24 to 26 (IP7)
@desc A consultation that was never requested: the Registrar or the Minister did not ask the Council
GIVETH A `Consultation of the Council`
`int — a consultation that was never requested` MEANS
    `Consultation of the Council` WITH
        `the function the consultation falls under` IS `function (3): advising the Registrar on individual applications and decisions`
        `a request for the Council's advice was made` IS FALSE
        `the source of the advice, if any has been given` IS NOTHING

§§ `Section 10(a): a measure against a licence`

@ref Law s.10(a), s.26(a)(3) (IP7)
@desc The facts of a measure under s.10(a) apart from the Council: the measure, the six grounds, the written hearing and the period; the consultation of the Council is a consultation record
DECLARE `Facts of a measure under section 10(a)` HAS
    `the measure` IS A `Measure under section 10(a)` @desc The measure the Registrar proposes
    `the grounds` IS A `Grounds under section 10(a)` @desc The six grounds, each a fact
    `the consultation of the Council` IS A `Consultation of the Council` @desc The consultation of the Council before the measure
    `the licensee was given an opportunity to make claims in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if, before the measure, the licensee was given the opportunity to make their claims in writing
    `the period of the restriction or suspension` IS A MAYBE `Period of a restriction or suspension under section 10` @desc The period of a restriction or suspension; NOTHING for a measure that has none

@ref Law s.10(a) (group 1), s.24 to 26 (group 4)
@desc Group 1's record of a measure under s.10(a), the two Council flags worked out by group 4 from the consultation
GIVEN f IS A `Facts of a measure under section 10(a)`
GIVETH A `Circumstances of a measure under section 10(a)`
`int — the circumstances of section 10(a) for` f MEANS
    `Circumstances of a measure under section 10(a)` WITH
        `the measure` IS f's `the measure`
        `the grounds` IS f's `the grounds`
        `the Council was consulted` IS `s 26 — the Council was consulted` (f's `the consultation of the Council`)
        `the Council's advice was validly given` IS `s 24 to 26 — the Council's advice was validly given` (f's `the consultation of the Council`)
        `the licensee was given an opportunity to make claims in writing` IS f's `the licensee was given an opportunity to make claims in writing`
        `the period of the restriction or suspension` IS f's `the period of the restriction or suspension`

@ref Law s.10(a), s.24 to 26 (IP7)
@export Whether s.10(a) lets the Registrar take the measure: the Council was consulted and its advice validly given (group 4), the licensee had the opportunity to make claims in writing, one of the six grounds is made out, and a restriction or suspension has a period of at most three years
GIVEN f IS A `Facts of a measure under section 10(a)` @desc The measure, the grounds, the consultation of the Council, the written hearing and the period
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`int — the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a) on` f MEANS
    `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a)` (`int — the circumstances of section 10(a) for` f)

@ref Law s.10(a), s.24 to 26 (IP7)
@export The preconditions of s.10(a) that are not met for the proposed measure, in group 1's order; empty if the Registrar may take it
GIVEN f IS A `Facts of a measure under section 10(a)` @desc The measure, the grounds, the consultation of the Council, the written hearing and the period
GIVETH A LIST OF `Unmet precondition of section 10`
`int — the preconditions of section 10(a) not met on` f MEANS
    `the preconditions of section 10(a) not met` (`int — the circumstances of section 10(a) for` f)

§§ `Section 10(b): suspension on an indictment`

@ref Law s.10(b), s.26(a)(3) (IP7)
@desc The facts of a suspension under s.10(b) apart from the Council
DECLARE `Facts of a suspension under section 10(b)` HAS
    `an indictment was filed against the licensee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if an indictment was filed against the licensee
    `in the Registrar's opinion the offence makes the licensee unfit to hold a licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Registrar's opinion (s.6(a)(3))
    `the Registrar saw that the gravity of the matter or the public interest requires the suspension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Registrar's finding
    `the consultation of the Council` IS A `Consultation of the Council` @desc The consultation of the Council before suspending
    `the licensee was given an opportunity to make claims in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the licensee was given the opportunity to make their claims in writing

@ref Law s.10(b) (group 1), s.24 to 26 (group 4)
@export Whether s.10(b) lets the Registrar suspend the licence until final judgment on the indictment, the Council's flags worked out by group 4 from the consultation
GIVEN f IS A `Facts of a suspension under section 10(b)` @desc The indictment, the Registrar's opinion and finding, the consultation of the Council and the written hearing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`int — the Registrar may suspend the licence until final judgment on` f MEANS
    `the Registrar may suspend the licence until final judgment`
        (`Circumstances of a suspension under section 10(b)` WITH
             `an indictment was filed against the licensee` IS f's `an indictment was filed against the licensee`
             `in the Registrar's opinion the offence makes the licensee unfit to hold a licence` IS f's `in the Registrar's opinion the offence makes the licensee unfit to hold a licence`
             `the Registrar saw that the gravity of the matter or the public interest requires the suspension` IS f's `the Registrar saw that the gravity of the matter or the public interest requires the suspension`
             `the Council was consulted` IS `s 26 — the Council was consulted` (f's `the consultation of the Council`)
             `the Council's advice was validly given` IS `s 24 to 26 — the Council's advice was validly given` (f's `the consultation of the Council`)
             `the licensee was given an opportunity to make claims in writing` IS f's `the licensee was given an opportunity to make claims in writing`)

§§ `Section 3(b): an exemption order`

@ref Law s.3(b), s.26(a)(1) (IP7)
@export Whether s.3(b) lets the Minister exempt classes of cooling systems by order: the Council was consulted and its advice validly given (group 4), and the Minister was satisfied that work on those classes carries no risk to safety
GIVEN consultation IS A `Consultation of the Council` @desc The consultation of the Council before the order
      `the Minister was satisfied that work on the classes carries no risk to safety` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Minister's opinion
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`int — the Minister may exempt classes of cooling systems by order after` consultation `with the Minister's satisfaction being` `the Minister was satisfied that work on the classes carries no risk to safety` MEANS
    `the Minister may exempt classes of cooling systems by order`
        (`Circumstances of an exemption order under section 3(b)` WITH
             `the Council was consulted` IS `s 26 — the Council was consulted` consultation
             `the Council's advice was validly given` IS `s 24 to 26 — the Council's advice was validly given` consultation
             `the Minister was satisfied that work on the classes carries no risk to safety` IS `the Minister was satisfied that work on the classes carries no risk to safety`
             `the Minister determined an exemption by the order` IS TRUE)

§§ `Section 17(b): a particular course`

@ref Law s.17(b), s.26(a)(3) (IP7, IP17)
@desc The facts of a requirement to attend a particular course apart from the Council: the days, the Registrar's findings, and whether the licensee attended and met its requirements
DECLARE `Requirement of a particular course under section 17(b)` HAS
    `the day of the course` IS A DATE @desc The day of the course the licensee was required to attend
    `the day notice of the requirement was given` IS A DATE @desc The day notice of the requirement was given to the licensee
    `the course was conducted by the Registrar or recognised by the Training Division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Registrar conducted the course or the Training Division recognised it
    `the consultation of the Council about requiring the course` IS A `Consultation of the Council` @desc The consultation of the Council before requiring the course
    `in the Registrar's opinion circumstances justify requiring attendance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Registrar's finding
    `in the Registrar's opinion attendance is required to train the licensee and to realise the purposes of the Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Registrar's finding
    `notice was given a reasonable time before the date of the course` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The judgement that the notice was given a reasonable time before the course
    `the licensee attended the course` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the licensee attended the course
    `the licensee met the requirements of the course` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the licensee met the requirements of the course

@ref Law s.17(b) (group 3), s.24 to 26 (group 4)
@desc Group 3's record of a particular course the Registrar required, the two Council flags worked out by group 4 from the consultation
GIVEN r IS A `Requirement of a particular course under section 17(b)`
GIVETH A `Particular course required under section 17(b)`
`int — the course required under section 17(b) by` r MEANS
    `Particular course required under section 17(b)` WITH
        `the day of the course` IS r's `the day of the course`
        `the day notice of the requirement was given` IS r's `the day notice of the requirement was given`
        `the course was conducted by the Registrar or recognised by the Training Division` IS r's `the course was conducted by the Registrar or recognised by the Training Division`
        `the Council was consulted about requiring the course` IS `s 26 — the Council was consulted` (r's `the consultation of the Council about requiring the course`)
        `the Council's advice about requiring the course was validly given` IS `s 24 to 26 — the Council's advice was validly given` (r's `the consultation of the Council about requiring the course`)
        `in the Registrar's opinion circumstances justify requiring attendance` IS r's `in the Registrar's opinion circumstances justify requiring attendance`
        `in the Registrar's opinion attendance is required to train the licensee and to realise the purposes of the Law` IS r's `in the Registrar's opinion attendance is required to train the licensee and to realise the purposes of the Law`
        `notice was given a reasonable time before the date of the course` IS r's `notice was given a reasonable time before the date of the course`
        `the licensee attended the course` IS r's `the licensee attended the course`
        `the licensee met the requirements of the course` IS r's `the licensee met the requirements of the course`
